# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Un singur indice de grup pe termen este impus {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "Tabloul de grupuri conține un indice pe termen, iar atribuirea unuia de altă lungime generează o eroare. Nimic din aval nu reverifică această invariantă, așa că ea este impusă acolo unde indicii intră în operator: un tablou prea scurt ar elimina în tăcere termenii finali, iar unul prea lung ar inventa grupuri pe care niciun termen nu le conține.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Ștergerea indicilor de grup prin atribuirea lui `None` este întotdeauna permisă.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "Cele două verificări sunt independente {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") raportează dacă coeficienții unui grup coincid, aceasta fiind presupunerea pe care o face [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") când face media magnitudinilor. Nu este o formă mai slabă a verificării hermiticității: niciuna dintre verificări nu o implică pe cealaltă, în niciun sens.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "În mod implicit se compară magnitudinile, deoarece aceasta este ceea ce mediază [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). O pereche conjugată hermitian cu coeficienți complecși are magnitudini egale, dar coeficienți diferiți, deci satisface doar forma implicită.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Notă\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") moștenește garanția unilaterală a lui [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): o intrare `True` este întotdeauna de încredere, în timp ce o intrare `False` este de încredere doar pentru tipurile de operatori a căror formă normală este o autentică formă canonică. Consultă tipul specific de operator pentru a afla care caz se aplică.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

